-- migration_085_seed_cvc_templates.sql
--
-- Slice #36.01 — the „Contract de Vânzare" and „Act Adițional" forms.
--
-- WHAT THIS DOES
-- --------------
-- Writes `template_fields` onto two rows of `lookup_document_type`. That is
-- all. It is a DATA migration: no column is added, no constraint is created,
-- nothing is dropped, and it can be re-run — the two UPDATEs are unconditional
-- writes of a literal, not merges.
--
-- WHY IT IS A MIGRATION AND NOT A FORM-EDITOR SESSION
-- ---------------------------------------------------
-- The template mechanism is deliberately data — „adding a new document type's
-- full template is a DB row, never a schema migration or a code deploy"
-- (migration_066, and template-fields.ts's header). That is a statement about
-- the SCHEMA, not a licence to leave a form in one database. A template typed
-- into Reference Data exists only there: `Verify-Rebuild.ps1` replays the
-- migration chain and `src/db/sync-reference-data.sql` seeds the reference
-- rows, and neither would know about it. So these two forms ship twice — here,
-- for a database that is migrated forward, and in `sync-reference-data.sql`,
-- for one that is rebuilt from scratch — and `src/__tests__/cvc-template.test.ts`
-- asserts the two copies are identical.
--
-- WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* A FIELD IN EITHER FORM
-- -------------------------------------------------
-- Four repeating groups that a notarial deed is mostly made of, because
-- `document.custom_fields` is `Record<string, string | null>` — one string per
-- key, flat — and there is no `useFieldArray` anywhere in `src/`. Expressed as
-- template fields they would need the `_2` / `_3` suffixes that finding F5 of
-- the #29.01 import report already produced once:
--
--   * PARTIES -> `person_document`, one row per person per role, with the
--     cotă-parte on the row (migration_084). One deed carries three buyers at
--     63,64 / 9,09 / 27,27 percent; another carries one man who is both a
--     seller in his own name and the mandatar of three others.
--   * OBJECT OF SALE -> `property`, through `property_document`. A type-4 deed
--     — a lot plus 10,41% of an access road — is TWO linked properties.
--   * THE SELLER'S TITLE CHAIN -> `document_document`, with a
--     `lookup_document_document_role`. Every event in a chain is an instrument
--     the catalogue already knows. A 2016 deed with reconstituire ->
--     moștenire -> partaj -> CVC anterior is four links, not four field sets.
--   * SUPPORTING CERTIFICATES -> the same mechanism. CERTIFICAT_FISCAL,
--     EXTRAS_CARTE_FUNCIARA, CERTIFICAT_SARCINI, PROCURA, ANTECONTRACT and
--     CERTIFICAT_URBANISM are all seeded types, and the act adițional's parent
--     CVC is one more link of the same kind.
--
-- That is also the arithmetic that makes the form fit. Folded back in, „Contract
-- de Vânzare" needs well over a hundred fields; left as associations the scalar
-- remainder is 53, under the 60 `MAX_TEMPLATE_FIELDS` allows.
--
-- ⚠️ **AN INSTRUMENT THE DEED *CITES* BUT THE ARCHIVE DOES NOT HOLD STILL HAS
-- NOWHERE TO GO, AND THAT IS KNOWN.** „Titlu de proprietate nr. N/zz.ll.aaaa,
-- CJSDPT X" cannot be a link when no such document row exists, and this
-- migration deliberately mints no `titluNr` / `titluData` fields as a stop-gap,
-- because a four-event chain would immediately need `_2`, `_3` and `_4` — F5
-- again. Until `Slice.36.03` ships, such a citation lands in `unmappedRaw` and
-- is folded into „Note extinse" by the ai-interpret route. That is the symptom
-- Adrian named, it is not closed here, and 36.03 is the slice that closes it.
--
-- ONE FORM FOR FIVE FLAVOURS, AND A SECOND FOR THE SIXTH
-- ------------------------------------------------------
-- Groups 1 to 5 of the archive differ by THE STATE OF THE PAPERWORK — no
-- cadastral number yet, a temporary /N land book, a later completion, a
-- compound object — which is a fact about one transaction, not a class of
-- document. So they share one form and „Categorie internă" records which
-- flavour a deed is (filterable for free: `customFieldFilter` and
-- `GET /api/documents/custom-field-values`, #34.10). Only group 6, the act
-- adițional, is a different instrument, and it already has its own type row.
--
-- NOTHING IS DROPPED
-- ------------------
-- Both rows carry `template_fields` NULL today — this is greenfield, not a
-- rewrite — so there is no `custom_fields` value anywhere in the archive that
-- these writes could orphan. Verified before writing:
--   SELECT key, template_fields IS NOT NULL FROM lookup_document_type
--    WHERE key IN ('CONTRACT_VANZARE', 'ACT_ADITIONAL');

SET client_encoding = 'UTF8';

-- ── „Contract de Vânzare" — 53 fields over 4 notebook tabs ────────────
UPDATE lookup_document_type
   SET template_fields = $cvc$
[
